{
  "_": [
    "The hinge between tools/tos_cp3/session_inputs.py (CP-3 plan 2026-10-10 \u00a73.6,",
    "PR-3) and the three runtime stores it reads. The firewall is bidirectional, so",
    "no single test can hold both ends: tools/ may not import tos_runtime, and a test",
    "under tos/ may not import tools. This file is what both halves read.",
    "",
    "reads  \u2014 every (table, column) the extractor selects.",
    "payloads \u2014 the EXACT payload_json bytes the REAL stores write, produced by",
    "  driving SqliteEvidenceStore through EngineEvidenceSinkAdapter and",
    "  SqliteEventInbox. PR-3 first cut read entries.payload_json as if it were the",
    "  engine record; the store wraps it ({\"payload\": .., \"masked_keys\": ..}), so",
    "  every field came back null and the tools-side tests missed it because they",
    "  wrote flat rows of their own invention. A fixture of invented bytes tests the",
    "  invention. These are the stores own.",
    "",
    "payloads.marketfeed_snapshots — three snapshots the REAL SqliteSnapshotStore",
    "  wrote, keyed by the FieldState shape each carries: valid / stale (a STALE",
    "  field evaluation) / unknown (an UNKNOWN evaluation over a STALE observation).",
    "  M5's first count reads field_evaluations[*].state out of these bytes, so a",
    "  fixture without a STALE one would exercise the counting path on nothing.",
    "payloads.inbox_events[*].handling_started_evidence_seq / consumed_evidence_seq",
    "  — written by the real mark_handling_started / mark_consumed. They are the",
    "  bracket a capsule-less decision record is attributed by; the VALUES here are",
    "  the shape a real EngineDriver run writes (asserted live, on a real driver, by",
    "  the tos-side test). The second tick also carries a real, non-null",
    "  ContextValueView — the surface the value-view counts read.",
    "",
    "tos side  \u2014 tos/runtime/tests/operations/test_cp3_session_store_reads.py:",
    "  the columns exist in the registered migrations, and these bytes are what the",
    "  stores write today (byte equality \u2014 regenerate in the PR that moves them).",
    "tools side \u2014 tests/tools/test_cp3_session_inputs.py: the extractor pins the same",
    "  versions, its fixture stores are built from exactly these columns, and the",
    "  evidence/inbox rows it parses are exactly these bytes."
  ],
  "marketfeed": {
    "file_name": "marketfeed.sqlite3",
    "schema_version": 1,
    "reads": {
